      "id": "hook",
      "chapter": "A dial attached to nothing",
      "narration": "This lock has a dial with forty numbers, and it opens for just one sequence of three. That's sixty-four thousand possible combinations. Yet the dial isn't connected to the latch at all. Spin it as much as you like, and nothing that holds this lock shut will move. So how does a dial that's attached to nothing know the right numbers?",
