    {
      "id": "pins",
      "chapter": "A chain of pins",
      "narration": "The cam is easy: it turns with the dial. But how can the dial move two wheels that aren't attached to it? With a chain of small pins. The cam has a drive pin on its back. Each wheel has a tab on its front, called a fly, and the front wheel has another pin on its back. Turn the dial, and the cam's pin travels around until it bumps into the front wheel's fly, and starts dragging the wheel along.",
