    {
      "id": "pickup",
      "chapter": "Why three turns",
      "narration": "Keep turning, and the front wheel's pin catches the back wheel. Now everything spins together. That's why you start by turning right several times: it gathers up every wheel, and wipes out whatever was set before. Then stop on the first number, thirty-five. The back wheel, the last one picked up, is now parked with its gate at the top.",
