    {
      "id": "second",
      "chapter": "The second number",
      "narration": "Now turn left. The cam's pin has to travel almost a full turn before it reaches the front wheel's fly from the other side. That's why you go past the first number once. From there, the front wheel moves with the dial, while the back wheel stays put, because nothing reaches it. Stop on six, and the front wheel's gate lines up too.",
      "step": "STEP 2   Turn LEFT, past 35 once, stop on 6",
